      "About $2.02 per 25 g at the Amazon price we saw, nearly double Carnivor",
      "21 g of protein per scoop, 2 g less than Carnivor",
      "Consumer Reports rated it for occasional use on lead in October 2025"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Pay more per gram for a cleaner, grass-fed label; read our Equip review for the lead context first.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "21 g (label)",
      "Calories": "About 100 to 110",
      "Third-party testing": "Brand-stated; no certification listing found",
      "Cost per 25 g": "About $2.02 (Amazon price seen)"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B013MRPPL6"
  },
  {
    "id": "carnivor-protein-powder-review-alt-transparent-labs-beef-isolate",
    "name": "Transparent Labs Beef Isolate Protein, Chocolate, 30 Servings",
    "brand": "Transparent Labs",
    "badge": "More Protein per Scoop",
    "category": "Hydrolyzed grass-fed beef protein isolate",
    "description": "Transparent Labs' beef isolate gives the most protein per scoop of the beef powders here: 25 g per serving of Chocolate, per its Amazon listing at the time of writing, 2 g more than Carnivor. It is naturally flavored, sweetened with stevia rather than sucralose, and made from grass-fed beef, per the brand, which also says it is third-party tested for heavy metals. We did not find an Informed Choice or NSF listing. At the $59.99 we saw on Amazon, it works out to about $2.00 per 25 g.",
    "pros": [
      "25 g of protein per scoop, per the listing",
