        <div id="taste-mixing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. What Do Buyers Say About Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Buyers are split on taste and mixing. On the 56-serving Chocolate listing, Amazon showed a 4.4 out of 5 average from 4,427 ratings when we checked, with 73 percent five-star and 8 percent one-star. Amazon's AI summary of the reviews says many customers find the taste and mixability good, while others find it unpleasant and hard to mix. We have not tasted it; everything in this section is buyer feedback.
          </p>

          <p>
            The most common praise is that Carnivor is a dairy-free protein that does not upset the stomach the way whey does for people with lactose intolerance. Reviewers who switched from whey often say this is the reason they stay. Several also call it one of the better-value proteins they have bought, which matches the cost math above.
          </p>

          <p>
            The most common complaints are foaming and clumping, a smell some describe as odd until the powder is mixed, and digestive trouble for a minority of buyers, including diarrhea. Some reviewers dislike the ingredient list, naming maltodextrin and sucralose specifically, and a few mention concerns about lead and bioengineered ingredients. Others say value has slipped as prices rose.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Which Carnivor flavor do buyers like best?</h3>

          <p>
            Chocolate is the default and the flavor with by far the most reviews, and buyers generally describe it as a safe choice. Amazon lists nine flavors: Chocolate, Chocolate Peanut Butter, Cinnamon Toast, Cookies and Cream, Fruit Punch, Fruity Cereal, Rocket Pop, Strawberry and Vanilla Caramel. The fruity flavors are the ones beef protein does best in, according to many beef-protein buyers generally, because they work well mixed with water like a juice drink, while creamy flavors can taste thin without milk.
          </p>

          <p>
            Mixing tips from reviewers are simple. Use cold water, add the powder after the liquid, and let the foam settle for a minute before drinking. A blender makes the foam worse, not better. Using 8 ounces of water rather than 6 reduces clumping for most people.
          </p>
        </div>

