                  Chocolate has by far the most buyer reviews and is generally described as the safe choice. Many beef-protein buyers also like the fruity flavors, such as Fruit Punch and Rocket Pop, because they taste like a juice drink when mixed with water. Creamy flavors can taste thin in water. These are buyer reports; we have not tasted Carnivor.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the most common complaints about Carnivor?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Buyer reviews most often mention foaming and clumping, an odd smell before mixing, and stomach upset or diarrhea for a minority of people. Others criticize the long ingredient list, particularly maltodextrin and sucralose, and some mention the Prop 65 lead warning or rising prices. Praise centers on lactose-free digestion, decent taste in Chocolate and good value.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Carnivor contain dairy, lactose or gluten?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  No dairy or lactose, per MuscleMeds, because the protein comes from beef rather than milk. The jar also says it is gluten-free, sugar-free and fat-free and contains no gelatin. It does list refined soybean oil in its antifoam blend, so anyone with a soy allergy should check the current label or ask MuscleMeds before buying.
                </p>
